<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African board says no sale on 15,000 T maize.</title>
<headline>S.African board says no sale on 15,000 T maize.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Maize Board said on Thursday there was no sale for the export or domestic use of 15,000 tonnes of yellow maize offered earlier this week.</p>
<p>The export tender closed late on Thursday.</p>
<p>The board said it had received only one tender from trading firm Andre-Genfood at $125.05 a tonne, but that it had not accepted it.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
